# clamav-daemon FHS migration: unify the split-brain on /var/run/clamav.
#
# This package shipped LocalSocket /run/clamav/clamd.sock while its
# own initd and unit created /var/run/clamav: the socket's directory
# was never created where the socket was configured. The socket path
# is corrected here; directory lifecycle (accounts.d dir stanza +
# tmpfiles.d) lives in the base clamav output that owns the
# clamav:120 identity - this package declares no identity it does
# not own.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - clamd socket: cleared at (re)start in both inits (tracked-start
#   only); the daemon recreates it. No daemon-side reclaim exists in
#   source, so service logic owns it.
# - Old /run/clamav: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once empty;
#   left in place and reported while old daemons run. (The same old
#   dir served freshclam; one removal declaration covers the shared
#   path - exact-path union refuses duplicates.)

rmdir-if-empty /run/clamav
